{"v":"sugar","rows":[{"cell":"a"}]}
a string: ok -> value: text

an int: ok -> value: 7

a float: ok -> value: 1.5

a big integer: ok -> value: 123456789012345678901

a true: ok -> value: true

a false: ok -> value: false

a decimal: ok -> value: 19.90

null: '@{v}' is null, and a hole holds text
an array: '@{v}' is an array, and a hole holds text
an object: '@{v}' is an object, and a hole holds text
rows from json: ok -> - x
- y

a row that is not an object: '@{r.cell}': 'cell' was read on a number
a for over an object: '@for r in rows' needs an array, and that is an object
a context that is an array: a template's context is a JSON object, and this one is an array
a context that is a string: a template's context is a JSON object, and this one is a string
expressions in holes: ok -> ADA L: 3 items
fallback nowhere
- 2
- 4
- 6

a hole over an absent key: '@{absent?.city ?: 'nowhere'}': no 'absent' here; this object has first, last, count, nothing, numbers
a cell read on a number: '@{r.cell}': 'cell' was read on a number
a binder shadowing a binding: '@for v in rows' would shadow the bound 'v'
a malformed hole: template line 2: 'a +' is not an expression: expression:4: expected a value, found the end of the expression
a @for with no source: template line 2: '@for' reads '@for <binder> in <expression>'
an empty context: '@{v}': no 'v' here; this object has no keys
a key nothing uses: 'extra' is bound and template 'one' never mentions it (it uses: v)
